NAHPU documentation is translated into Brazilian Portuguese, Spanish, and
Indonesian with AI assistance and reviewed by people. This page is the shared
reference for how NAHPU and natural history terms are rendered in each
language, so the same concept does not appear under three different names.

{% aside type="note" %}
This page is available in English only. Translation is coordination work
between languages, so it stays in one place.
{% /aside %}

## Rules

### On-screen names stay in English

The NAHPU interface is English-only. When a sentence names a control the reader
must find on screen — a button, a field label, a menu entry, a card title —
write it in English inside backticks and translate the prose around it:

```text
en  Select `Add taxon`, then choose the `Import` mode.
pt  Selecione `Add taxon` e escolha o modo `Import`.
es  Seleccione `Add taxon` y elija el modo `Import`.
id  Pilih `Add taxon`, lalu pilih mode `Import`.
```

Do not translate the text inside the backticks. A reader who is looking for a
translated button will not find one.

When the same word is used as an ordinary noun rather than as the name of a
control, translate it: `Site ID` stays in English, but "record the site
coordinates" becomes "registre as coordenadas do local".

### Scientific terms follow the receiving language

Taxonomic ranks, Latin names, and collection vocabulary have established forms
in each language. Use them. Leaving `class`, `order`, `family`, and `epithet` in
English inside an Indonesian sentence is not more precise — it is harder to
read for the person the translation is for.

Italicize genus and species names in every language, and never translate them.

### Standards keep their published names

`Darwin Core`, `dwc:scientificName`, `dwc:MaterialEntity`, `dwc:preparations`,
GBIF, IUCN, CITES, ORCID, UUID, and file formats such as `.xlsx`, `JSON.GZ`, and
`TAR.GZ` are proper names. Never translate them, and never translate a
`dwc:` term into a local phrase in running text.

### Do not invent a term

If a concept has no settled equivalent, keep the English term in backticks and
explain it once in the receiving language. Add the decision to the table below
so the next translator makes the same choice.

## NAHPU concepts

| English | Portuguese (BR) | Spanish | Indonesian |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| project | projeto | proyecto | proyek |
| site (the place) | local | sitio | lokasi |
| `Site` (the record type) | `Site` | `Site` | `Site` |
| locality | localidade | localidad | lokalitas |
| location (project scope) | localização | ubicación | wilayah |
| collecting event | evento de coleta | evento de recolecta | kegiatan pengumpulan |
| effort | esforço | esfuerzo | upaya |
| specimen | espécime | espécimen | spesimen |
| specimen part | parte do espécime | parte del espécimen | bagian spesimen |
| parasite | parasita | parásito | parasit |
| host | hospedeiro | hospedador | inang |
| narrative | narrativa | narrativa | narasi |
| record | registro | registro | catatan |
| field (in a form) | campo | campo | kolom |
| controlled vocabulary | vocabulário controlado | vocabulario controlado | kosakata terkontrol |
| field ID | ID de campo | ID de campo | ID lapangan |
| project ID | ID do projeto | ID del proyecto | ID proyek |
| media | mídia | medios | media |
| backup | backup | copia de seguridad | cadangan |
| restore | restauração | restauración | pemulihan |
| export | exportação | exportación | ekspor |
| import | importação | importación | impor |
| preset | predefinição | preajuste | prasetel |
| template | modelo | plantilla | templat |
| user configs | configurações de usuário | configuraciones de usuario | konfigurasi pengguna |

## People and roles

| English | Portuguese (BR) | Spanish | Indonesian |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| personnel | pessoal | personal | personel |
| cataloger | catalogador | catalogador | pengatalog |
| collector | coletor | colector | pengumpul |
| preparator | preparador | preparador | preparator |
| determiner | determinador | determinador | pengidentifikasi |
| collecting personnel | pessoal de coleta | personal de recolecta | personel pengumpul |

Role names that appear in the personnel form — `Cataloger`, `Determiner only`,
`Preparator only`, `None` — are on-screen names. Keep them in English inside
backticks and use the translated word in prose.

## Taxonomy

| English | Portuguese (BR) | Spanish | Indonesian |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| taxon / taxa | táxon / táxons | taxón / taxones | takson |
| taxonomy | taxonomia | taxonomía | taksonomi |
| taxon rank | categoria taxonômica | categoría taxonómica | tingkat takson |
| kingdom | reino | reino | kerajaan |
| phylum | filo | filo | filum |
| class | classe | clase | kelas |
| order | ordem | orden | ordo |
| family | família | familia | famili |
| genus | gênero | género | genus |
| species | espécie | especie | spesies |
| subspecies | subespécie | subespecie | subspesies |
| specific epithet | epíteto específico | epíteto específico | epitet spesifik |
| subspecific epithet | epíteto subespecífico | epíteto subespecífico | epitet subspesifik |
| scientific name | nome científico | nombre científico | nama ilmiah |
| authorship | autoria | autoría | kepengarangan |
| common name | nome comum | nombre común | nama umum |
| identification | identificação | identificación | identifikasi |

{% aside type="caution" title="Indonesian ranks" %}
Use `ordo` and `famili`, not `order` and `family`. Use `takson` and `spesimen`,
not `taxon` and `specimen`. Earlier translations left these in English; they are
being corrected as pages are revised.
{% /aside %}

